OL,3,GNEWSARenovated chapel granted wedding
OL,4,Alicence
OL,5,
OL,6,FA once run-down Victorian chapel in
OL,7,FCoventry renovated with lottery cash
OL,8,Fhas been granted a wedding licence.
OL,10,FThe Grade II listed Anglican building
OL,11,Fon London Road was built in 1847, but
OL,12,Ffell into disrepair, before being
OL,13,Frestored by Historic Coventry Trust
OL,14,F(HCT) and Coventry City Council.
OL,16,FSitting within the Paxton Arboretum and
OL,17,Finitially used for funeral services, it
OL,18,Fwas designed by Sir Joseph Paxton -
OL,19,Fbest known for creating Crystal Palace
OL,20,F- alongside his assistants George
OL,21,FRobertson and George Henry Stokes.
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
